// Compiler-owned relationship between provider-backed opaque semantics and a
// concrete physical representation. A named implementation names both as
// ordinary trait arguments: `Opaque` is the boundary-opaque declaration and
// `Representation` is the checked-shape data it is laid out as. The relationship
// is inert until the authoritative build selects one exact named implementation.
// Selection does not import representation cleanup: v1 admits only a
// compiler-proven inert closed representation, while the opaque declaration
// remains the sole semantic lifecycle authority. The representation, not
// source-authored ABI numbers, supplies layout.

pub trait OpaqueRepresentation<Opaque, Representation> {
}
